<edge source="hormuz_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="ai_governance_crisis::enterprise_adoption_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained, effective blockades that disrupt shipping create operational pressures that push firms to accelerate procurement and integration of AI-driven supply‑chain automation, routing optimization, and resilience tools to maintain operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="hormuz_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="currency_activism_shocks::net_capital_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A successful blockade that materially constrains trade and export receipts reduces sovereign and corporate cashflows and raises perceived country risk, prompting portfolio re‑allocations away from affected jurisdictions and producing net capital outflows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="hormuz_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">An effective chokepoint blockade heightens immediate energy and trade security concerns for European and Asian governments, prompting political pressure to soften or delay strict enforcement of sanctions (including on energy) to stabilize markets and supply, reducing overall sanctions rigor toward actors in the Russia‑Ukraine context.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="hormuz_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="russia_ukraine_war::munitions_stock_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A successful blockade compels NATO and partner states to reallocate limited munitions and air/maritime defense stocks to regional escorts and partner defense, slowing or reducing transfers and stock replenishment available for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="hormuz_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A more effective chokepoint blockade that restricts outbound/inbound cargo directly prevents delivery of critical fab equipment, specialty gases and wafers to affected fabs, forcing production curtailments and reducing installed semiconductor capacity in the impacted jurisdiction.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
