<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="ai_governance_crisis::capital_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger sanctions enforcement blocks cross‑border payments, freezes assets, and increases compliance costs and legal risk, causing financiers and vendors to pull or reallocate investment away from affected AI projects and geographies, reducing net capital flows into those AI activities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="currency_activism_shocks::net_capital_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter and more effectively enforced sanctions restrict access to foreign banking and investment channels for targeted actors and counterparties, triggering immediate capital flight and a drop in inbound portfolio and banking flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="currency_activism_shocks::pol_pressure_monetary" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger sanctions raise domestic price shocks, fiscal burdens, and liquidity squeezes that prompt elected officials to pressure central banks for rate cuts, credit lines, or asset‑support operations to blunt political fallout.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="hormuz_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter, more comprehensive sanctions on Russia push Moscow to deepen security and arms cooperation with Iran (including transfers and operational support), increasing the capacity and willingness of Iranian-aligned actors to conduct maritime attacks in Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger sanctions enforcement builds enforcement institutions, intel/sharing channels and legal precedents that governments extend to broader, tighter export controls on dual‑use and advanced technologies.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
