<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="ai_governance_crisis::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls create new cross‑border compliance rules and reporting requirements that force regulators to expand surveillance, audits and pre‑deployment checks of AI systems to ensure sanctions and licensing rules are met.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="ai_governance_crisis::capital_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened export restrictions raise geopolitical and compliance risk for investors, prompting withdrawal or redirection of funding away from cross‑border AI projects and lowering net capital flows into affected AI development chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="currency_activism_shocks::net_capital_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden increase in export controls raises regulatory and segmentation risk for targeted firms and sectors, provoking rapid portfolio reallocation and withdrawals by foreign investors which reduce net cross‑border capital inflows to the affected jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="currency_activism_shocks::market_volatility_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export restrictions create immediate uncertainty about supply chains, earnings and trade exposures that triggers rapid repricing across equities, bonds and FX, elevating short‑term market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="hormuz_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter US export controls escalate Sino‑US strategic competition, prompting China to deepen security/arms cooperation with Tehran and encourage or enable Iran-aligned maritime harassment (via equipment, training, or tacit coordination), which raises the rate of attacks on vessels tied to US/allied interests.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::munitions_stock_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter export controls block or delay Russia's access to dual‑use semiconductors, guidance sensors and precision components, directly slowing production and repair of guided munitions so inventories fall as attrition outpaces replacement.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::unmanned_weapons_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter controls on imaging chips, navigation modules and RF parts disrupt supply chains for loitering munitions and tactical UAVs, reducing the rate at which those systems can be produced, resupplied and launched in operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
